  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "The numbers \\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) \\(z\\) are proportional to \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(5.\\) The sum of \\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) and \\(z\\) is \\(100.\\) The number \\(y\\) is given by the equation \\(y=ax-10.\\) Then \\(a\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac52\\)",
    "E": "\\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The ratio \\(x:y:z=2:3:5\\) divides the total into \\(2+3+5=10\\) equal parts. Since the total is \\(100\\), each part is \\(100/10=10\\). Therefore \\(x=20\\), \\(y=30\\), and \\(z=50\\).\n\nSubstitute \\(x=20\\) and \\(y=30\\) into the given equation:\n\\[\n30=20a-10\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n40=20a\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\na=2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
